Spec: Map

Purpose:
  The live MapLibre map for riding, following and ride detail, and the pre-rendered ride previews
    that History lists without any live map.

Owns:
  ./live_map.dart
  ./map_attribution.dart
  ./map_config.dart
  ./openfreemap.dart
  ./openfreemap_tile_provider.dart
  ./preview_projection.dart
  ./preview_snapshot.dart
  ./route_camera.dart
  ./route_marker_painter.dart
  ./route_preview_cache.dart
  ./route_preview.dart
  ./route_sketch.dart
  ./tile_grid.dart
  /test/map

References:
  /docs/specs/history/07-map-system.md
  /docs/specs/history/16-maplibre-live-map.md
  /docs/specs/history/19-openfreemap.md
  /docs/specs/history/map-notes.md
  /lib/domain/route_markers.sdd
  /lib/domain/heading.sdd

Must:
  The live map is native MapLibre with the bundled Retrail Light or Retrail Dark style, handed over as an
    asset path, never as a JSON string.
  Android uses the texture platform-view mode so no stale native surface flashes between screens.
  The ride map follows the position heading-up from recorded points; a user gesture drops follow and the
    recenter control restores it; the compass shows while the map is not north-up.
  Every follow or recenter move requests the ride zoom; the very first position jumps instantly.
  The detail and fullscreen map frames the whole route with @fitRouteCamera, north-up, without a compass,
    and moves the same map between dialog and fullscreen.
  Until the style has loaded a @RouteSketch of the route shows, so the route is visible offline.
  A followed reference is drawn below the live route, with its ridden parts greyed on top, and is pushed
    only into sources the current style load created.
  Every map shows the OpenMapTiles and OpenStreetMap credit through @MapAttribution, always written out.
  Start, finish and loop markers and direction arrows look the same on the live map, the sketch and the preview.
  Ride previews are rendered once when a ride is saved, in both light and dark, cached as PNG keyed by ride id
    and brightness, and shown with `Image.file`.
  A preview saved offline is a flat sketch, marked stale and re-rendered when back online; edit and delete evict it.
  Preview tiles are OpenFreeMap vector tiles drawn with `vector_tile_renderer` in the same bundled styles,
    zoom capped at `16`, sending `User-Agent: Retrail (io.github.valijuu.retrail)`.
  The preview cache directory carries a version; bumping it re-renders every preview and purges older versions.
  Projection math stays pure and tested.

Must not:
  Put a live map into a list item.
  Use the package's `fitBounds()` for framing, which iOS cancels.
